    "visualReview": "Full-size inspection of the supplied 896×1200 JPEG, the real-alpha checker, the 1600×2400 composition and the 400×600 preview: every organ in the source is present (button with veil; two standing fruit bodies with scaly caps, hanging white rings and scurfy stipes in mossy needle litter; inverted specimen with free dark-brown gills and a flaring ring; longitudinal section with white flesh, free gills and a slightly swollen base; moss, needles, two small cones, and a blue-green spruce sprig with a hanging cone). The existing cursive Gemini mark is complete and unaltered at bottom right. Pale cap, stipe and section interiors are opaque. Source RGB in the artwork is unchanged. Paper has been removed around the group; a soft irregular edge of cream remains in the litter clump where needles sit on the original paper, which is expected and is not a rectangular double frame. Uniform scale, no stretching, no repainting, no added signature. Anatomy is consistent with the species (fibrillose tawny-brown scales, hanging ring, scurfy stipe, free brown gills, spruce-fir litter). The plate is apparently AI-generated in a historical style; rights are unverified; the Gemini mark is a metadata credit only and is not proof of a human artist.",
